# First run and project changes

## When you need it

Start this **{{.training_layout}}** project with **{{.engine}}** training and
**{{.inference_mode}}** inference. Run commands beside `databricks.yml`.
This template pins `skyulf-core[mlflow]==0.9.3` in `deployment/requirements.txt`;
public guides describe the current revision. Before changing the pin, follow
[Upgrade an existing project](https://www.skyulf.com/manual/user_guide/databricks_project_upgrade.html)
and **Upgrade steps for generated Databricks projects** in the
[release notes](https://github.com/flyingriverhorse/Skyulf/blob/master/changelog/0.9.x.md).

## What to edit

[README.md](README.md) maps every setting to its file and guide. Before the first run,
set the target host and namespaces in `deployment/`. Monitoring runs only when
`deployment/variables.yml` names a monitoring catalog and schema.

Source tables and record-key columns must already exist. Set an absolute
`quality_threshold` before training if you intend to approve the first champion.
Quick setup accepts editable defaults; detailed setup asks applicable choices.

## The command

Replace `YOUR_PROFILE` with the authenticated profile for the selected target.

```powershell
uv pip install -r deployment/train-requirements.txt
python src/tools/smoke.py
python src/tools/preview.py --action train
databricks bundle validate --strict -t {{if eq .personal_development_targets "true"}}test_development{{else}}test{{end}} --profile YOUR_PROFILE
databricks bundle deploy -t {{if eq .personal_development_targets "true"}}test_development{{else}}test{{end}} --profile YOUR_PROFILE
databricks bundle run -t {{if eq .personal_development_targets "true"}}test_development{{else}}test{{end}} --profile YOUR_PROFILE train
```

Inspect the concrete candidate and decision before running `score` with the same
target/profile. If training already started a child score run, inspect it first.
For first-time monitoring of an unactivated pinned candidate, prepare its
reference before scoring: [reference preparation](https://www.skyulf.com/manual/user_guide/databricks_monitoring_enrollment.html).

## What you should see

{{if eq .training_layout "multi_target"}}Open `train_<name>`, `training_report` (`models_report.py`) and `model_decision`.
The set has one complete pinned release; review all components before activation.
{{else if eq .training_layout "model_competition"}}Open candidate fits, `select_best_model` and `training_report`. Only the selected
winner receives protected holdout comparison; a failed winner does not promote a runner-up.
{{else}}Open `train_and_tune` and `training_report`. Registration alone does not activate a candidate.
{{end}}Start with **Where to look** in `training_report` > Output. Copy an **Available action**
or **If rollback is needed** block into the train job's **Run now with different parameters**:
[operator actions](https://www.skyulf.com/manual/user_guide/databricks_lifecycle.html#operator-actions-through-run-now).
Inspect committed score output, then `monitoring_report` and `evaluate_retraining`.
Dashboard refresh displays saved measurements; it does not calculate new ones.

## Common errors and fixes

Smoke and preview check local configuration, not source data or workspace access.
A downstream monitoring failure does not undo committed predictions. Start with
the first failing task and record its run ID, target and model/set version.

